        "original_id": "fe7de4e3-4d0a-5071-a163-a570d967f7c7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Frances Sweeney, Charles Edward Coughlin\n- Places: Boston, Detroit, Royal Oak, Michigan\n- Organizations: National Shrine of the Little Flower church, Boston Herald\n- Products: Boston City Reporter, Rumor Clinic\n- Roles: journalist, activist, Roman Catholic priest\n- Topics: fascism, antisemitism, political corruption, fascist disinformation\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Edward Coughlin was born on October 25, 1891, and died on October 27, 1979.\n- Charles Edward Coughlin was a controversial Canadian-American Roman Catholic priest based near Detroit at the National Shrine of the Little Flower church in Royal Oak, Michigan.\n- Frances Sweeney was born around 1908 and died on June 19, 1944.\n- Frances Sweeney was a journalist and activist who campaigned against fascism, antisemitism, and political corruption in 1940s Boston.\n- Frances Sweeney edited her own newspaper, the Boston City Reporter.\n- Frances Sweeney started the Boston Herald Rumor Clinic to combat fascist disinformation.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
